# ArkHive message catalog: install as /usr/lib/systemd/catalog/arkhive.catalog,
# then run journalctl --update-catalog. journalctl -x shows these explanations.

-- 038e5a6f18f6184144c8b36819606286
Subject: ArkHive backup started
Defined-By: arkhive
Documentation: https://github.com/mauriziofonte/arkhive#logging

The backup of the configured paths and database dumps to the restic repository started (arkhive backup, run @ARKHIVE_RUN_ID@).
Every event of this run carries ARKHIVE_RUN_ID=@ARKHIVE_RUN_ID@; the run ends with a
succeeded or a failed event.

-- 763619ea04f7dbbf790ad973e212db7a
Subject: ArkHive backup succeeded
Defined-By: arkhive
Documentation: https://github.com/mauriziofonte/arkhive#logging

The backup of the configured paths and database dumps to the restic repository ended with exit status @ARKHIVE_EXIT_STATUS@:
0 is a success, 3 a success with warnings (logged before this event).

-- 0dca6b902c5ac3d8b27d93e0ffcc4c5e
Subject: ArkHive backup failed
Defined-By: arkhive
Documentation: https://github.com/mauriziofonte/arkhive#logging

The backup of the configured paths and database dumps to the restic repository failed with exit status @ARKHIVE_EXIT_STATUS@.

The status is a sysexits(3) code: 64 usage, 65 data error (a check or a drill
found damage), 66 missing input, 69 unavailable (repository, server or tool
unreachable), 73 output refused, 74 I/O error (disk full), 75 temporary (lock
held, deadline passed: the next run may succeed), 77 permission denied,
78 configuration error, 130 or 143 interrupted, 1 any other failure.

The error and its hint are the events before this one with the same
ARKHIVE_RUN_ID=@ARKHIVE_RUN_ID@: journalctl ARKHIVE_RUN_ID=@ARKHIVE_RUN_ID@.
`arkhive doctor` checks the whole setup.

